  "finding": "TypedRelationBlock.__post_init__ bounded and semantically validated values but always rebuilt them with tuple(...), even when _from_indexed, matmul, or hadamard had already supplied an exact immutable canonical tuple. This duplicated the retained CSR value container after construction.",
  "gardener_change": "Validate each scalar exactly once, keep the existing tuple when every validated scalar is already the stored representation, and allocate a fallback list/tuple only when the caller supplied a non-tuple sequence or scalar normalization changes an item. No helper cache, alternate block type, index, store, registry, scheduler, backend, graph authority, semantic plane, or public product surface was added.",
  "focused_regressions": [
    "A canonical Boolean values tuple is retained by exact object identity after TypedRelationBlock validation.",
    "A Tropical integer tuple still falls back to a newly normalized float tuple, proving identity reuse cannot bypass scalar normalization."
